  "question": "The ratio of the interest received when Rs. (x + 500) is invested at 32% p.a. simple interest for 4 years to the interest received when Rs. (x - 500) is invested at 20% p.a. compound interest, compounded annually for 2 years, is 64 : 11. Find the value of 'x'.",
