  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nPrincipal 1 = x + 500\n\nRate 1 = 32%\n\nTime 1 = 4 years\n\nPrincipal 2 = x − 500\n\nRate 2 = 20%\n\nTime 2 = 2 years\n\nRatio of interests = 64 : 11\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nSimple Interest = (P × R × T) ÷ 100\n\nCompound Interest = P[(1 + R/100)ⁿ − 1]\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ SI = (x + 500) × 32 × 4 ÷ 100\n\n⇒ SI = (x + 500) × 128 ÷ 100\n\n⇒ SI = (x + 500) × 1.28\n\n⇒ CI = (x − 500)[(1.2)² − 1]\n\n⇒ CI = (x − 500)(1.44 − 1)\n\n⇒ CI = (x − 500) × 0.44\n\n⇒ Ratio = (1.28(x + 500)) ÷ (0.44(x − 500)) = 64 ÷ 11\n\n⇒ (32(x + 500)) ÷ (11(x − 500)) = 64 ÷ 11\n\n⇒ 32(x + 500) = 64(x − 500)\n\n⇒ 32x + 16000 = 64x − 32000\n\n⇒ 16000 + 32000 = 64x − 32x\n\n⇒ 48000 = 32x\n\n⇒ x = 48000 ÷ 32\n\n⇒ x = 1500\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 1500.**",
